{"id": "npcarlsbad", "name": "Carlsbad Caverns National Park", "short": "Carlsbad Caverns", "place": "New Mexico, USA", "lat": 32.15, "lon": -104.56, "side": "r", "cont": "North America", "country": "United States of America", "states": ["New Mexico"], "kind": "Desert", "park": true, "blurb": "Bats leave the cave at dusk and feed a Chihuahuan Desert web of hawks and snakes.", "tip": {"id": "bat", "title": "Silence the bat flight", "text": "The free-tailed bats eat moths and other insects over the desert at night. Set Mexican free-tailed bat to -100% and watch the moths, then the hawks and other animals that rely on them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Carlsbad Caverns National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlsbad_Caverns_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Mexican free-tailed bat", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexican_free-tailed_bat"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Chihuahuan Desert", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chihuahuan_Desert"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Cave swallow", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_swallow"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Western diamondback rattlesnake", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_diamondback_rattlesnake"}, {"title": "NPS: Carlsbad Caverns nature and science", "url": "https://www.nps.gov/cave/learn/nature/index.htm"}], "notes": "The story and why it matters come from the Wikipedia articles listed below (Carlsbad Caverns National Park, Mexican free-tailed bat, Chihuahuan Desert). Individual species and links have not been checked one by one. Feeding links that match a GloBI (Global Biotic Interactions) record are marked in the node details, with a link to the records. A few links were added from GloBI records.", "imgwiki": "Carlsbad Caverns National Park", "icon": "quad", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "creosote", "sp": "larrea tridentata", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "The dominant shrub on gravelly desert flats across the Chihuahuan Desert. Doves and finches are recorded eating its seeds.", "ic": "sage", "badge": "Foundation species"}, {"id": "lechuguilla", "sp": "agave lechuguilla", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "A spiky agave that Wikipedia names as an indicator plant of the Chihuahuan Desert. The park's famous Lechuguilla Cave is named after it.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "cholla", "sp": "cylindropuntia imbricata", "xh": 0.5, "name": "Tree cholla", "ic": "sage"}, {"id": "apache", "sp": "fallugia paradoxa", "xh": 0.72, "ic": "willow"}, {"id": "moths", "sp": "lepidoptera", "xh": 0.06, "ic": "mayfly"}, {"id": "deer", "sp": "odocoileus hemionus", "xh": 0.2, "wiki": "Mule deer", "desc": "Browses shrubs such as Apache plume. A common large herbivore of the desert and canyons."}, {"id": "aoudad", "sp": "ammotragus lervia", "xh": 0.34}, {"id": "woodrat", "sp": "neotoma leucodon", "xh": 0.5}, {"id": "kangaroo", "sp": "dipodomys merriami", "xh": 0.66, "desc": "A seed-eating desert rodent that is prey for hawks and rattlesnakes in GloBI records.", "ic": "gsquirrel"}, {"id": "dove", "sp": "zenaida asiatica", "xh": 0.84, "desc": "One of the most recorded birds near the park. GloBI records it eating creosote bush, and hawks and snakes prey on it."}, {"id": "bat", "sp": "tadarida brasiliensis", "xh": 0.04}, {"id": "swallow", "sp": "petrochelidon fulva", "xh": 0.16}, {"id": "gmouse", "sp": "onychomys arenicola", "xh": 0.28}, {"id": "lizard", "sp": "crotaphytus collaris", "xh": 0.44}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes velox", "xh": 0.6}, {"id": "vulture", "sp": "cathartes aura", "xh": 0.78, "wiki": "Turkey vulture", "desc": "Scavenges carcasses of deer, snakes and birds across the park. GloBI records many of these."}, {"id": "hawk", "sp": "buteo jamaicensis", "xh": 0.3, "wiki": "Red-tailed hawk", "desc": "A top aerial predator with a very wide diet in GloBI records, from kangaroo rats and lizards to rattlesnakes and bats.", "ic": "hawk"}, {"id": "rattler", "sp": "crotalus atrox", "xh": 0.62, "tl": 4, "desc": "Ambush predator that eats mostly small mammals such as kangaroo rats and 