talus atrox"], "dove>vulture": ["g", "Cathartes aura", "Zenaida asiatica"], "deer>hawk": ["ga", "Buteo jamaicensis", "Odocoileus hemionus"]}, "story": "Carlsbad Caverns National Park in southeastern New Mexico sits in the Guadalupe Mountains. Its Big Room is almost 4,000 feet long and 255 feet high at most, the largest chamber in North America. Sulfuric acid dissolved the limestone to form the caverns.", "matters": "About two-thirds of the park is wilderness, which protects its habitat. Gypsum in the cave shows how sulfuric acid shaped it."}